This PR aims to add the feature Magic Square, which validates if a given matrix is a Magic Square or not by calling `MagicSquare.validate(square)`.

- The `validate(square)` method receives a matrix and validates for it being a square, having all rows sums to the same value (by mathematical definition, all rows will sums to the same value as well) and having all diagonals sums to the same value;
- validation for being a square takes into account same number of rows and columns;
- validation for rows sums to the same value takes into account the sum value of the first row all the way until the last one and compare if all of them are the same;
- validation for diagonals sums to the same value takes into account the sum value of main diagonal (same row number and same column number) and compare if is the same from secondary diagonal (left to right column X right to left row);
  - to check for the right to left row we are using Ruby array manipulation, that goes for negative numbers to catch last position at -1 and going all the way to the first when reaching negative total rows count, always subtracting one by iteration.

### Description

This PR is a carry forward of https://github.com/MatrixAI/Polykey/pull/582

In the aforementioned PR, there were changes made to `PolykeyClient` to encapsulate `WebsocketClient` in. 

```ts
...
  const webSocketClient = await WebSocketClient.createWebSocketClient(
      {
        host,
        port,
        config: {
          verifyPeer: true,
          verifyCallback: async (certs) => {
            await clientUtils.verifyServerCertificateChain([nodeId_], certs);
          },
          keepAliveTimeoutTime: optionsDefaulted.keepAliveTimeoutTime,
          keepAliveIntervalTime: optionsDefaulted.keepAliveIntervalTime,
        },
        logger: logger.getChild(WebSocketClient.name),
      },
      ctx,
    );
...
constructor({
    nodePath,
    webSocketClient,
    rpcClient,
    session,
    fs,
    logger,
  }: {
    nodePath: string;
    webSocketClient: WebSocketClient;
    rpcClient: RPCClient<typeof clientClientManifest>;
    session: Session;
    fs: FileSystem;
    logger: Logger;
  }) {
    this.logger = logger;
    this.nodePath = nodePath;
    this.webSocketClient = webSocketClient;
    this.rpcClient = rpcClient;
    this.session = session;
    this.fs = fs;
  }
```

And further changes were made to the launch options for both `PolykeyClient `and `PolykeyAgent`

```ts
type PolykeyClientOptions = {
  nodePath: string;
  keepAliveTimeoutTime: number;
  keepAliveIntervalTime: number;
  rpcCallTimeoutTime: number;
  rpcParserBufferSize: number;
};


type PolykeyAgentOptions = {
  nodePath: string;
  clientServiceHost: string;
  clientServicePort: number;
  agentServiceHost: string;
  agentServicePort: number;
  seedNodes: SeedNodes;
  workers: number;
  ipv6Only: boolean;
  keys: {
    passwordOpsLimit: PasswordOpsLimit;
    passwordMemLimit: PasswordMemLimit;
    strictMemoryLock: boolean;
    certDuration: number;
    certRenewLeadTime: number;
    recoveryCode: string;
  };
  client: {
    keepAliveTimeoutTime: number;
    keepAliveIntervalTime: number;
    rpcCallTimeoutTime: number;
    rpcParserBufferSize: number;
  };
  nodes: {
    connectionIdleTimeoutTime: number;
    connectionFindConcurrencyLimit: number;
    connectionConnectTimeoutTime: number;
    connectionKeepAliveTimeoutTime: number;
    connectionKeepAliveIntervalTime: number;
    connectionHolePunchIntervalTime: number;
    rpcCallTimeoutTime: number;
    rpcParserBufferSize: number;
  };
};
```

This PR replicates these changes in Polykey-CLI by removing ws imports and usages, changing `PolykeyClient `signatures and adjusting the options accordingly.

Initially, `PolykeyClient `and `WebSocketClient `were initialized as such: 

```ts
        webSocketClient = await WebSocketClient.createWebSocketClient({
          config: {
            verifyPeer: true,
            verifyCallback: async (certs) => {
              await clientUtils.verifyServerCertificateChain(
                [clientOptions.nodeId],
                certs,
              );
            },
          },
          host: clientOptions.clientHost,
          port: clientOptions.clientPort,
          logger: this.logger.getChild(WebSocketClient.name),
        });
        pkClient = await PolykeyClient.createPolykeyClient({
          streamFactory: () => webSocketClient.connection.newStream(),
          nodePath: options.nodePath,
          logger: this.logger.getChild(PolykeyClient.name),
        });
        await binUtils.retryAuthentication(
          (auth) =>
            pkClient.rpcClientClient.methods.agentLockAll({
              metadata: auth,
            }),
          auth,
```

These are now changed to:

```ts
pkClient = await PolykeyClient.createPolykeyClient({
          nodeId: options.nodeId,
          host: options.clientHost,
          port: options.clientPort,
          options: {
            nodePath: options.nodePath,
          },
          logger: this.logger.getChild(PolykeyClient.name),
        });
        await binUtils.retryAuthentication(
          (auth) =>
            pkClient.rpcClient.methods.agentLockAll({
              metadata: auth,
            }),
          auth,
...
```

As `rpcClient `is called on `pkClient`, it already have access to the encapsulated `WebSocketClient`.

