I had trouble yesterday running 'python manage.py collectstatic.'  This is because 'STATIC_ROOT' was not defined in settings.py.  For now, I commented out 'STATICFILES_DIRS' and set STATIC_ROOT =  = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, "static").  After I did this, I was able to run the command.

Also, I left the original function clean_email intact.  I commented out the ValidationError for the purposes of creating more dummy accounts and uncommented those lines later:

    def clean_email(self):
        email = self.cleaned_data.get("email")

        if User.objects.filter(email=email).exists():
            raise ValidationError("Email already in use.")
        if not email.endswith("@nyu.edu"):
            raise ValidationError("Please use your NYU email.")
        return email

